\newlabel{fig:maps}{{7}{14}{Selectivity maps over 16 coordinates and 25 denoising steps (\texttt {mm} = motion module, \texttt {sp.a2x} = spatial cross-attention). Left: $S_{dyn}$ on the frame-varying part. Right: $S_{stat}$ on the frame mean. Blue is content-selective, orange motion-selective. Only \texttt {up0.mm2} (and \texttt {mid.mm0} in $\xs $) is motion-selective, and only in the first steps.\relax }{figure.caption.7}{}}
